    "long_instructions": "# Modify: Check Before You Move\r\n\r\nYour Task: This painter is facing south, and a traffic cone is right in front of it. The program tells the Painter to move anyway. Make the program handle the cone.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Run the program. What happens when the Painter moves into the cone? Read the error message.\r\n2. Add an `if` so the Painter only moves when `can_move()` is True. Run it again. What happens now? Why does the Painter just stand there?\r\n3. Add an `else` branch that makes the Painter turn when it can't move.\r\n4. Use Validate to check your work.",
